## No single number
The "eight glasses" rule is a rough idea, not a medical target. Needs depend on weather, activity, body size and diet.

## Simple signals
Thirst and pale-yellow urine are practical signs that you are drinking enough.

## Other sources
Tea, milk, fruit, vegetables and soups also add to your fluid intake.

## What to watch
Drink more in hot weather and during exercise. If you have kidney or heart conditions, or take medicines that affect fluids, ask your doctor how much is right for you.
